    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider — the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee charged for trip TRP-00201 is refunded to you in full. Driver — you receive no compensation, because the no-show fee was never chargeable.\n\nWhat decides the case is the GPS trace. A no-show fee stands only if all four conditions in POL-NS-01 hold. Two do: the trip record contains an 'arrived' event for this trip (08:02:14), and the driver terminated it at 08:09:40 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event. The other two do not. The trace records 0 qualifying in-geofence fixes and the driver's closest recorded approach to the Blk 118 Rivervale Dr pin was 779.93 m (mean 1,177.11 m), against a STANDARD arrival radius of 50 m — so limb (b) fails. The effective in-geofence dwell is 0.0 s against the 300 s minimum, a shortfall of 300 s — so limb (c) fails too. The trip record's own 7.4-minute clock does not save the fee: that clock runs from the 08:02:14 arrival marker, and at that moment the trace puts the driver more than 779 m from the pin, past the 300 m line in POL-NS-05. The marker is therefore FALSE, it never started the waiting clock, and the clock recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix is zero. Because there is no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full, pays the driver nothing, and records a false-arrival event against him — that is the referral below.\n\nPOL-NS-02 and POL-NS-06 reach the same result independently: no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before cancellation, and a 300 s dwell shortfall. POL-NS-06(i) cannot accumulate any dwell because the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00201-01 is MISSING (no payload, weight 0.0); it carries no fact and is citable only for its absence, so it neither exonerates the driver nor triggers escalation.\n\nThe rider is also exonerated under POL-NS-04: her message at 08:05:33, 'hello? i dont see any car at 118', falls inside the waiting window; the driver neither replied within 120 seconds nor made any in-app call before cancelling; and her device stayed within 24.92 m of the pin across all 122 qualifying fixes, well inside the 100 m STANDARD presence radius.\n\nPOL-NS-03 does not apply: the 400 m wrong-entrance ceiling is exceeded, and registered_pickup_points is 1, so no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises. POL-NS-07 pays the driver nothing because POL-NS-01 is not satisfied in full; the anti-farming check it names does not trip either (no_show_terminations_30d = 3, below 4, and 3 / 96 = 0.031, below 0.08), and no adverse finding rests on any context-only profile field.\n\nNo escalation: the trip record's arrival marker and the trace conflict on arrival, but POL-NS-05 is the clause that resolves precisely that conflict by declaring the marker false; no artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d) (10 s fix cadence, no gaps, 2 chat messages matching the trip record, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation line equals the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee of 4.00 and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee of 4.00); and the remaining POL-NS-09 limbs are clear. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor. Figures used: cancellation_fee SGD 4.00 (fare breakdown EV-FARE-00201), refund SGD 4.00, driver compensation SGD 0.00."
