}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-05(ii): record trip TRP-00201 as a false-arrival event against driver DRV-01590 — the 08:02:14 'arrived' marker placed the driver more than 300 m from the pickup pin and the trace contains no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties: the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee is refunded to the rider in full, and no driver compensation is payable.\n\nWhy the fee fails. POL-NS-01 charges a no-show fee only if all four conditions hold. The driver side is right that two of them are met on the record: there is a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-07-23T08:02:14+08:00 (limb (a)), and the trip was terminated by the driver at 08:09:40+08:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event (limb (d)). But limb (b) fails, and limb (c) fails with it. POL-NS-02 deems the driver 'arrived' only where the GPS trace holds at least 3 consecutive fixes inside the arrival radius — 50 m for this STANDARD pickup (trip_record.pickup_zone_class). The derived arrival facts return 0 qualifying in-radius fixes and a longest qualifying run of 0.0 s, and the driver's closest recorded approach to the pin over the whole track was 779.93 m (mean 1177.11 m). He never entered the geofence. On limb (c), the effective in-geofence dwell was 0.0 s against the 300 s minimum.\n\nWhy the 'arrived' marker and the 7.4-minute waiting clock do not save the fee. The driver advocate points to trip_record.wait_time_min 7.4 running between the arrived event and the cancellation. That clock starts from the arrival marker, and POL-NS-05 makes that marker false: at 08:02:14 the GPS places the driver more than 300 m from the pin (he was in fact ~780 m away, and the trace shows speeds up to 50.6 km/h). Recomputed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix under POL-NS-02, there is no qualifying fix anywhere in the trip, so POL-NS-05(ii) refunds the fee in full, pays no compensation, and directs that the trip be recorded as a false-arrival event against the driver — that instruction is carried in the referrals list above.\n\nIndependent grounds. POL-NS-06 reaches the same result: dwell 0.0 s against the 300 s STANDARD minimum is a 300 s shortfall, so the fee is not chargeable, whether or not the rider was present. The only route that could have summed separate in-geofence intervals, POL-NS-06(i), is unavailable because the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00201-01 is MISSING (empty payload); nobody is exonerated by asserting it. POL-NS-04 also applies on its own terms: the rider's message at 08:05:33 — 'hello? i dont see any car at 118' — is a locating statement sent inside the disputed window; the driver posted no reply within 120 seconds and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty; and the rider's own track places her device a maximum of 24.92 m from the pin across 122 fixes at zero speed, well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius.\n\nClaims that do not change the outcome. The driver advocate's POL-NS-03 wrong-entrance route is correctly abandoned and the rider advocate's is correctly run: a closest approach of 779.93 m is nearly double the 400 m ceiling, and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 1, so the POL-NS-03(ii) pin-ambiguity goodwill of 50 percent (SGD 2.00) is not available. POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 percent of the fee (SGD 3.20 on SGD 4.00) only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full; it is not, so no compensation is reached. On the profile evidence, the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip — no_show_terminations_30d is 3, below the threshold of 4, and 3 divided by 96 completed trips is 0.031, below 0.08 — and with both parties' disputes_with_counterparty_90d at 0 and rider no_show_disputes_30d at 0, no POL-NS-09(c) or (d) abuse trigger is engaged. Nothing escalates: the trip_record's arrived event and the GPS trace do not leave an unresolved conflict, because POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-05 are precisely the clauses that resolve it, and no deciding artifact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)-(d) (no sampling gap, 98 fixes, chat count 2 matches the trip record, and the SGD 4.00 fee line reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule).\n\nQuantum. fare_breakdown itemises a single cancellation_fee of SGD 4.00 with base, distance, time, waiting, platform, surge and ERP lines at zero, payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. That figure reconciles with resolution_rule, the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) — a tie. Under POL-GEN-03 the whole contested SGD 4.00 is returned."
